error[K0025]: Kobo cannot use this ownership hint
  --> tests\ui\K0025_hint_ignored.kobo:4:30
  |
4 |     #[kobo::hint(ownership = "move")]
  |                              ^^^^^^ this ownership hint asks Kobo to move `buf`
5 |     let buf = String::from("kobo");
  |         --- hint applies to this value
  |
What Kobo found:
  The hint asks Kobo to move `buf`, but the code mutably uses `buf` more than once.
Why this matters:
  A moved value has only one owner. This code needs a shape that can support repeated mutable use.
Try this:
  Remove the hint, change it to match the sharing pattern, or refactor so `buf` has only one owner.
More:
  Run `kobo explain K0025` for examples and deeper context.
  Also: if this sharing is intentional, let Kobo choose the shared representation and review it with
  `kobo inspect`
